# Intent: styles.css has no content hash in its name and there is no build
# step, so a CSS change cannot be versioned by URL. Revalidating it means a
# change reaches a returning visitor immediately, and the ETag keeps the usual
# case a 304 with no body.
#
# STATUS: THIS RULE IS CURRENTLY OVERRIDDEN AND HAS NO EFFECT.
#
# Measured 2026-10-28, after deploying this file (wrangler logged
# "Uploading _headers"):
#
#   sincerelycozy.com/styles.css   public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate
#   sincerelycozy.com/blog/        public, max-age=0,     must-revalidate
#   getranklabs.com  (static)      public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate
#   getranklabs.com/robots.txt     public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate
#
# Cloudflare documents the Pages default as max-age=0, must-revalidate, so the
# four-hour value is not coming from Pages. It appears on static assets across
# two separate zones while HTML passes through untouched, which is the
# signature of a zone-level Browser Cache TTL of 4 hours applied at the edge.
# A zone setting wins over whatever the origin sends, so this file cannot fix
# it.
#
# To actually fix it, one of:
#   1. Cloudflare dashboard -> the zone -> Caching -> Configuration ->
#      Browser Cache TTL -> "Respect Existing Headers". Then this file starts
#      working. Account-level change, so it needs a human.
#   2. Version the stylesheet in markup (styles.css?v=N) and bump N whenever
#      the CSS changes. Fully in-repo, but every page and the blog post
#      template must carry the same N.
#
# Kept rather than deleted so the rule is already correct if option 1 is taken.
# Do not treat the presence of this file as the problem being solved.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
